ts under which we license intellectual property rights from third parties or otherwise experience disruptions to our business relationships with our licensors, we could lose license rights that are important to our business.","context":"•If we are unable to maintain intellectual property protection, our competitive position could be harmed; and","section":"•Changes in U.S. trade policy and the impact of tariffs may have a material adverse effect on our business, results of operations and financial condition.","block":412,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001274737-26-000009","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-03-10","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001274737","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1274737/000127473726000009/exdx-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/3cc8854c4453f1b25ff224b51ebe08cde468b2958b7b2186c6157a7da0e735b8.bin","sha256":"3cc8854c4453f1b25ff224b51ebe08cde468b2958b7b2186c6157a7da0e735b8"}},{"id":"942b2a08eb33a6de96de8a07ed21b3ba1aa99ab9fd2ed0519867de829d5bfd1b","quote":"We have a history of losses, we expect to incur net losses in the future and we may not be able to generate sufficient revenue to achieve and maintain profitability.","context":"Risks Related to Our Business and Strategy","section":"•Changes in U.S. trade policy and the impact of tariffs may have a material adverse effect on our business, results of operations and financial condition.","block":414,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001274737-26-000009","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-03-10","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001274737","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1274737/000127473726000009/exdx-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/3cc8854c4453f1b25ff224b51ebe08cde468b2958b7b2186c6157a7da0e735b8.bin","sha256":"3cc8854c4453f1b25ff224b51ebe08cde468b2958b7b2186c6157a7da0e735b8"}},{"id":"fd7ec72e5ab3d0a44cd613cee3d35d75398c24973d00f2a5605cf704dbec5f69","quote":"We have incurred net losses since our inception. For the years ended December 31, 2025 and 2024, we incurred net losses of $20.0 million and $15.1 million, respectively, and we expect to continue to incur additional losses in 2026 and in future periods. As of December 31, 2025, we had an accumulated deficit of $314.3 million. We also expect to continue to devote substantial resources to increase adoption of, and reimbursement for, our testing products and to develop future testing products. Over the next several years, we expect to continue to devote substantially all of our resources to increase adoption of, and reimbursement for, our testing products and to develop future testing products. We may not be able to generate sufficient revenue to achieve and maintain profitability. Our failure to achieve and maintain profitability in the future could cause the market price of our common stock to decline and materially and adversely affect our prospects and business.","context":"We have a history of losses, we expect to incur net losses in the future and we may not be able to generate sufficient revenue to achieve and maintain profitability.","section":"•Changes in U.S. trade policy and the impact of tariffs may have a material adverse effect on our business, results of operations and financial condition.","block":415,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001274737-26-000009","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-03-10","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001274737","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1274737/000127473726000009/exdx-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/3cc8854c4453f1b25ff224b51ebe08cde468b2958b7b2186c6157a7da0e735b8.bin","sha256":"3cc8854c4453f1b25ff224b51ebe08cde468b2958b7b2186c6157a7da0e735b8"}},{"id":"76573557b6455bb3159bcc4fbb81bc4b7b0c135e63ea8147e0a0965a3501729a","quote":"If third-party payors do not provide coverage and adequate reimbursement for our testing products, or they breach, rescind or modify their contracts or reimbursement policies or delay payments for our testing products, or if we or our partners are unable to successfully negotiate payor contracts, our commercial success could be materially compromised.","context":"We have incurred net losses since our inception. For the years ended December 31, 2025 and 2024, we incurred net losses of $20.0 million and $15.1 million, respectively, and we expect to continue to incur additional losses in 2026 and in future periods. As of December 31, 2025, we had an accumulated deficit of $314.3 million. We also expect to continue to devote substantial resources to increase adoption of, and reimbursement for, our testing products and to develop future testing products. Over the next several years, we expect to continue to devote substantially all of our resources to increase adoption of, and reimbursement for, our testing products and to develop future testing products. We may not be able to generate sufficient revenue to achieve and maintain profitability. Our failure to achieve and maintain profitability in the future could cause the market price of our common stock to decline and materially and adversely affect our prospects and business.","section":"•Changes in U.S. trade policy and the impact of tariffs may have a material adverse effect on our business, results of operations and financial condition.","block":416,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001274737-26-000009","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-03-10","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001274737","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1274737/000127473726000009/exdx-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/3cc8854c4453f1b25ff224b51ebe08cde468b2958b7b2186c6157a7da0e735b8.bin","sha256":"3cc8854c4453f1b25ff224b51ebe08cde468b2958b7b2186c6157a7da0e735b8"}},{"id":"c202abdb80476d3e5b22a5d4202549fe0751e559c6ddd473385bbdaca56056a8","quote":"Successful commercialization, or continued commercialization, of our testing products depends, in large part, on the availability of coverage and adequate reimbursement from third-party payors, including government payors, such as Medicare and Medicaid and commercial payors. For the testing products that we develop and commercialize, each third-party payor decides whether to cover the product, the amount it will reimburse for a covered product and the specific conditions for reimbursement.","context":"If third-party payors do not provide coverage and adequate reimbursement for our testing products, or they breach, rescind or modify their contracts or reimbursement policies or delay payments for our testing products, or if we or our partners are unable to successfully negotiate payor contracts, our commercial success could be materially compromised.","section":"•Changes in U.S. trade policy and the impact of tariffs may have a material adverse effect on our business, results of operations and financial condition.","block":417,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001274737-26-000009","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-03-10","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001274737","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1274737/000127473726000009/exdx-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/3cc8854c4453f1b25ff224b51ebe08cde468b2958b7b2186c6157a7da0e735b8.bin","sha256":"3cc8854c4453f1b25ff224b51ebe08cde468b2958b7b2186c6157a7da0e735b8"}},{"id":"fbac0917de9ba55b0d09f100d0f6d5e94626d905a9567ad7f335cbcbdbf921e6","quote":"Reimbursement by third-party payors may depend on a number of factors, including the payor’s determination that tests using our technologies are:","context":"Successful commercialization, or continued commercialization, of our testing products depends, in large part, on the availability of coverage and adequate reimbursement from third-party payors, including government payors, such as Medicare and Medicaid and commercial payors. For the testing products that we develop and commercialize, each third-party payor decides whether to cover the product, the amount it will reimburse for a covered product and the specific conditions for reimbursement.","section":"•Changes in U.S. trade policy and the impact of tariffs may have a material adverse effect on our business, results of operations and financial condition.","block":418,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001274737-26-000009","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-03-10","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001274737","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1274737/000127473726000009/exdx-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/3cc8854c4453f1b25ff224b51ebe08cde468b2958b7b2186c6157a7da0e735b8.bin","sha256":"3cc8854c4453f1b25ff224b51ebe08cde468b2958b7b2186c6157a7da0e735b8"}},{"id":"0d5a2edc7f0e4835ea4efecb857d00813c9165f5f589b072cea8d1962a9ad866","quote":"•demonstrated to lead to improved patient outcomes;","context":"•medically necessary;","section":"•Changes in U.S. trade policy and the impact of tariffs may have a material adverse effect on our business, results of operations and financial condition.","block":421,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001274737-26-000009","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-03-10","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001274737","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1274737/000127473726000009/exdx-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/3cc8854c4453f1b25ff224b51ebe08cde468b2958b7b2186c6157a7da0e735b8.bin","sha256":"3cc8854c4453f1b25ff224b51ebe08cde468b2958b7b2186c6157a7da0e735b8"}},{"id":"09288da10877afd621c69b53296e3f21b345901975cef1b6a97ca82bdc6d39c5","quote":"•supported by peer-reviewed medical journals; and","context":"•cost-saving or cost-effective;","section":"•Changes in U.S. trade policy and the impact of tariffs may have a material adverse effect on our business, results of operations and financial condition.","block":424,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001274737-26-000009","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-03-10","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001274737","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1274737/000127473726000009/exdx-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/3cc8854c4453f1b25ff224b51ebe08cde468b2958b7b2186c6157a7da0e735b8.bin","sha256":"3cc8854c4453f1b25ff224b51ebe08cde468b2958b7b2186c6157a7da0e735b8"}},{"id":"20983662bbadd47f54801c280e2782e1ae2cf2317a0b284cda0cfd4da25b5c66","quote":"If we are unable to provide third-party payors with sufficient evidence of the clinical utility and validity of our tests, they may not provide coverage, or may provide limited coverage, which may materially and adversely affect our revenue and our ability to succeed. In addition, clinicians may be less likely to order a test unless third-party payors pay a substantial portion of the test price. Therefore, coverage determinations and reimbursement levels and conditions are critical to commercial success, and if we are not able to secure positive coverage determinations and reimbursement levels, our business may be materially adversely affected.","context":"•included in clinical guidelines.","section":"•Changes in U.S. trade policy and the impact of tariffs may have a material adverse effect on our business, results of operations and financial condition.","block":426,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001274737-26-000009","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-03-10","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001274737","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1274737/000127473726000009/exdx-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/3cc8854c4453f1b25ff